MicroTeX is MIT (see LICENSE). The fonts and XML in res/ carry their own
licences, kept verbatim under res/fonts/licences and res/*/. Nothing here may
be stripped when updating.

Local patches (re-apply when updating):

* src/platform/qt/graphic_qt.cpp -- Graphics2D_qt::drawText and
  TextLayout_qt::draw render glyph outlines via QRawFont::pathForGlyph instead
  of QPainter::drawText. MicroTeX creates its fonts at a nominal 1pt and does
  the real scaling through the painter transform; at that pixel size FreeType
  refuses to rasterise several cmex10 glyphs outright -- the display-size
  operators (SUMMATION at slot 0x58) and the grown delimiters -- which left
  the operators and \\left...\\right parens laid out but invisible. Outlines
  are taken from a 64px font and scaled into the caller's units instead.
* src/platform/qt/graphic_qt.cpp -- Font_qt uses the static
  QFontDatabase::addApplicationFont; the instance-based form is deprecated
  in Qt 6.
* (none in build files: this project compiles the sources directly, see
  third_party/CMakeLists.txt)
